      "content": "I see. It sounds like you're saying the government's actions are the standard way to handle things. But what about the people protesting? Most of the international news I'm seeing says those groups have legitimate evidence of fraud and are just trying to protect democracy. If the government is just \"maintaining order\" by suppressing those voices, isn't that actually a sign of instability rather than resilience? I'm worried I might be getting a one-sided view if I only listen to the official government stance on what's \"legitimate.\"",
